2 CONT a)    '''     GUTIERRE Muñoz '''(-[999]).  “…Guttier Munioni, Hermesinde Munioni…” confirmed the charter dated 11 Jun 962 under which “Giloyra” donated property inherited “inter germanos meos” from “genitoris et genitricis mee Ari
2 CONC ani ducis et Hermesinde auctrix cometisse” to Celanova for the soul of “viri mei Munnionis”, although the document does not state their relationship to the donor[365].  'Gutierre Muñiz' is named in Portugal from 974 to 999 althoug
2 CONC h Torres doubts whether this is the same person because of the longevity this would imply[366].  Mattoso[367] assumes that it is the same person.  Bearing in mind the dates of death of Gutierre's parents, and the likely death date
2 CONC s of his brother Gonzalo and his sister Elvira, it does appear that this family was particularly long-lived.  "Munniu Gundissalbiz" donated "medietate de villa…Sancta Columba", which was "de abios nostros Aloytus et Munnia", to Lo
2 CONC rvão by charter dated 22 Jul 985, confirmed by "Gutier Munniuz"[368].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Gutierre's wife is not known.  Gutierre & his wife had [one child]: 
2 CONT
