1 NOTE Rey de León (955-958) y (960-966)
1 NOTE King of Leon 956-958, then assumed throne again from 960 to 966.
2 CONT In 966 he was murdered, (poisoned by Galician nobles.)
1 NOTE Sancho I also called "The Fat" succeeded Ordono III El Bueno, to the throne of Leon in 956.  His reign was short-lived, and ended in 958. He was succeeded by Ordono IV el Malo.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Ordono IV el Malo died in 960, Sancho I the Fat, or El Grasso, resumed the throne until he died in 967.  He was succeeded by Ramiro III.
