1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvira_Men%C3%A9ndez_de_Melanda
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00120382&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes de Melanda (c. 996 - 1022), foi condessa de Portugal e rainha consorte de Leão (1014-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Era natural da Galiza e filha de Tutadona Moniz e do conde Mendo Gonçalves, conde do primeiro condado de Portucale, co-regente de Leão durante a menoridade de Afonso V, seu genro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira casou-se em 1014 com Afonso V de Leão, donde nasceram:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Bermudo III de Leão (c. 1015-1037), rei de Leão;
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Sancha I de Leão (1013-1067), rainha titular de Leão e rainha consorte de Castela, casada em 1032 com Fernando I de Castela.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elvira_Mendes
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes, sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia, (c. 996 – 20 December 1022), was Queen of León (1008-1022). Daughter of Count Mendo Gonçalves II of the First County of Portugal (House of Vímara P
2 CONC eres) and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was the mother of King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband, Alfonso V of León, Elvira had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Bermudo III of León (c.1015-1037)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Sancha of León (c.1020-1067), married Ferdinand I of León
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT The Royal Ancestry Bible, Royal Ancestors of 300 Colonial American Families Vol. 3 (chart 2186) by Michel L. Call ISBN 1-933194-22-7
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira Mendes, sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia, (c. 996 – 20 December 1022), was Queen of León (1008-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Count Mendo Gonçalves II of the First County of Portugal (House of Vímara Peres) and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was 
2 CONC the mother of King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband, Alfonso V of León, Elvira had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Bermudo III of León (c.1015-1037)
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Sancha of León (c.1020-1067), married Ferdinand I of Leon
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Elvira Mendes, sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia, (c. 996 – 20 December 1022), was Queen of León (1008-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Count Mendo Gonçalves II of the First County of Portugal (House of Vímara Peres) and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was 
2 CONC the mother of King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
2 CONT By her husband, Alfonso V of León, Elvira had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bermudo III of León (c.1015-1037) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha of León (c.1020-1067), married Ferdinand I of León
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sometimes called 'Geloria Menendez' of Portugal or Galicia.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Elvira Mendes de Melanda''' (c. 996 - 1022), foi condessa de Portugal e rainha consorte de Leão (1014-1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT Era natural da Galiza e filha do conde Mendo Gonçalves, conde do primeiro condado de Portucale, e de Tutadona Moniz, o qual foi co-regente de Leão durante a menoridade de Afonso V, seu genro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elvira casou-se em 1014 com Afonso V de Leão, donde nasceram:
2 CONT
2 CONT *    Bermudo III de Leão (c. 1015-1037), rei de Leão;
2 CONT *    Sancha I de Leão (1013-1067), rainha titular de Leão e rainha consorte de Castela, casada em 1032 com Fernando I de Castela.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reina consorte por su matrimonio con el rey Alfonso V de León. Era hija del conde Menendo González y la condesa Mayor. Su padre, hijo del conde Gonzalo Menéndez dux magnus de Portugal, fue, junto con la reina Elvira García, regent
2 CONC e y tutor del rey Alfonso V de León con quien Elvira contrajo matrimonio en 1015.
2 CONT
2 CONT De su matrimonio con el rey Alfonso V nacieron dos hijos: Bermudo III de León (1017-1037). Sucedió a su padre en el trono. Sancha de León (1016-1067). Contrajo matrimonio con el rey Fernando I el Magno, rey de Castilla y León, hij
2 CONC o de Sancho III el Mayor, rey de Pamplona.
2 CONT
2 CONT Falleció el día 2 de diciembre del año 1022 y recibió sepultura en el Panteón de Reyes de San Isidoro de León. El sepulcro de piedra en el que fue depositado el cadáver de la reina se conserva en la actualidad, y en su cubierta ap
2 CONC arece esculpida la siguiente inscripción latina: H. R. REGINA DOMNA GELOIRA UXOR REGIS ADEFONSI FILIA MELENDI COMITIS. OBIIIT III NON. DEC....JACET HAC IN FOSSA GELOIRAE REGINAE PULVIS ET OSSA PROLES MENENDI, ET TUK, QUAE OBIIT II
2 CONC II. NON. DEC. ERA LX POST M.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth: 	unknown, Spain Death: 	Dec. 20, 1022, Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT Born around 996 sometimes called Elvira or Geloria Menéndez of Portugal or Galicia was Queen of León (1008–1022).
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Count Menendo González of the First County of Portugal and corregente of León, descendant of the highest nobility of Portugal and Galicia, she married Alfonso V of León (before 1010). She was the mother of 
2 CONC King Bermudo III of León.
2 CONT
