1 NOTE alcaide-mor de D. Sancho [1154-1211, reigned 1185-1211]
2 CONT
2 CONT The information of Fr. Ariz in Hist6ria das Grandesas de Àvila gives the sequence of names as Esteban Domingo --> Joannes Esteban --> Ivanez Esteban --> Blasco Munoz --> Esteban Domingo --> Joannes Esteban --> Ivanez Esteban --> B
2 CONC lasco Munoz --> Esteban Domingo --> Blasco Munoz --> Martin Munoz . The first four names are repeated exactly. The only difference is that the later Ivanez is called Ivanez Esteban de Villa Franca, which might be an understandable
2 CONC  variation of the same person's name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Esteban Domingo was "alcaide em 1307." To achieve that station he must have been born before 1290, more probably 1280. Martin Munoz was "alcaide-mor de D. Sancho" who lived 1154-1211, reigned 1185-1211. If Martin Munoz was born in
2 CONC  1150, that makes 130-140 years between him and his great-great-great-great-great-great-great-great-grandson. This is only possible if each son was born when the father was 14 years of age. This seems almost impossible.
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe that these four individuals are duplicates. If they are merged, then Esteban is only Martin's great-great-great-great-grandson. This makes the difference of 130-140 yeas more reasonable since it allows about 23 years bet
2 CONC ween each generation. This is more normal. I have merged these individuals based on this reasoning. Obviously, more research needs to be done to determine which line is correct
1 CHAN
2 DATE 20 MAR 2022
3 TIME 03:03:24
