1 NAME Suero /Bermúdez/ conde y señor de Montaos
2 GIVN Suero
2 SURN Bermúdez
2 NSFX conde y señor de Montaos
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1130
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Regarding the "legendary" lineage of Suero Bermúdez, Fernando Bermúdez de Castro y Ozores writes: ''At the end of the 17th century Pedro Álvarez de Vega, then Marqués de Montaos, commissioned the ''Genealogical Mem
2 CONC orial of the House of the Counts of Grajal and the houses incorporated in it'''. The author of the Memorial already warned that '''it is not easy to hit the point of certain truth, when historians are so diverse in referring to it
2 CONC s origin'''. However, the succession proposed in that Memorial has been considered valid even in the 20th century.'' Which, simplified, would be:
2 CONT
2 CONT I.- Suero Bermúdez II.- Bernardo Bermúdez III.- Adán Bermúdez IV.- Lope Bermúdez V.- Pedro Bermúdez Prego VI.- García Prego de Montaos VII.- Pedro Bermúdez, "The Old Man"
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Fernando continues: "Although it is obvious, it seems that we still have to remember it: not all those who use the same last name have to be relatives and, much less, have to belong to the same lineage." See the genealogy prop
2 CONC osed by don Fernando according to his most recent and painstaking documentary-based research in:<br/>
2 CONT http://genealogiabermudezdecastro.es/BERMUDEZ-DE-MONTAOS/
2 CONT
