2 CONT 1.        ''' DIEGO López''' (-1124).  "Filiis meis Didaco, Sancie et filia Tota et Santia et Taresa" confirmed the donation by "Tecla comitissa filia Didaco Albaroyz" for the soul of "comitis de Lupi de Alaua et Bizcaya mariti me
2 CONC i" by charter dated Jan 1094[373].  He succeeded his father in [1093] as Señor de Vizcaya.  "Domna Tecla cometissa…cum filiis meis" donated property to the monastery of San Millán de Cogollo by charter dated 1093, which names "dom
2 CONC nus meus Lupus comes et eius pater Enneco Lopez" and is confirmed by "Didaco Lupez et frater meus Sancio Lupez et meus cognatus senior Gundissalvez Lupe et domna Tota et dompna Sancia et domna Tarasia, meis sororibus"[374].  "Domn
2 CONC a Ticlo cometissa" chose to be buried in the monastery of San Millán de la Cogolla by charter dated 1104, naming "meus pater Didaco Alvarez", and witnessed by "filios meos…Tota Lopez, Sancia Lopez, Didaco Lopez, Sancio Lopez, Tere
2 CONC sa Lopez…"[375].  Señor de Nájera.  Señor de Haro.  Alfonso VI King of Castile granted him the town of Haro in Rioja[376].  Three charters dated 1110, under which various property was donated or sold to the monastery of Santa Marí
2 CONC a de Valbanera, name "… Didacus Lupus dominante in Nagera et in Grannone…" in the dating clause directly following the names of the monarchs[377].  "Urraca…tocius Ispanie regina" confirmed rights of the monastery of San Millán de 
2 CONC la Cogolla by charter dated Aug 1110, confirmed by "…Didacus Lopiz senior in Nagera…"[378].  The dating clause of a charter dated Aug 1116, under which Alfonso I King of Aragon donated the monastery of San Martín de Soto to Valvan
2 CONC era, records “quando Didaco Lopiz erat in guerra cum rege iam dicto Adefonso”[379].  “Didago Lopiz meo germano y sua uxor Maria Sancii, senior Garcia Lopiz de Galinero cum sua uxore Goda Lopiz” witnessed the charter dated 1121 und
2 CONC er which “Tota Lopiz cum filia mea Maria Lopiz” donated property “nostram hereditatem…iuxta Angustiana…Sotihori” to Santa María la Real de Nájera, for the souls of “parentum nostrorum Lupi comitis et Tecle comitisse et Lupi Gonsal
2 CONC vez”[380].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MARÍA Sánchez, daughter of SANCHO Sánchez [de Navarra] Señor de Erro y Tafalla & his [second] wife ---.  “Tota Lopiz cum filia mea Maria Lopiz” donated property “nostram hereditatem…iuxta Angustiana…Sotihori” to Santa Marí
2 CONC a la Real de Nájera by charter dated 1121, witnessed by “Didago Lopiz meo germano y sua uxor Maria Sancii…”[381].  Her parentage is indicated by the charter dated to [1127] under which "Comes Santius [de Erro]" donated property to
2 CONC  Santa María de Pamplona for the soul of "patris et matris mee et sororis Sancie" which confirms that he had no male child by his wife but names "filiorum meorum aliquis…vel Egidius vel Raimirus vel Didaco Lopeys"[382], it being a
2 CONC ssumed that "Didaco Lopeys" was Sancho's son-in-law not his son.
2 CONT
