1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_%C3%81lvares_Pereira
2 CONT
2 CONT Dom Pedro Álvares Pereira (13?? – 14 August 1385) was a Portuguese noble of the 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Iria Gonçalves do Carvalhal and Álvaro Gonçalves Pereira, to whom he succeed after his death as patriarch of the Pereira family and as Prior of Crato (leader of the Knights Hospitaller in Portugal). He was the ol
2 CONC der brother of the Constable of Portugal, Dom Nuno Álvares Pereira.
2 CONT
2 CONT He became an ally of Dona Leonor Teles, and during the Portuguese crisis of 1383–1385 he supported the claims to the Portuguese throne of John I of Castile, who would nominate him Master of the Castilian Order of Calatrava.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fighting for John I of Castile, he participated in the Battle of Atoleiros where he was defeated by his brother, Nuno Álvares Pereira, and was one of the few survivors from the Castilian army. In the Battle of Aljubarrota he led a
2 CONC  Castilian charge against the Portuguese rearguard, but he died soon after while running away from his brother's army.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_%C3%81lvares_Pereira
