2 CONC cy. Champion of the papacy and in secret league with the Lombard cities he was able to defy the common enemy, Frederick I Barbarossa. In 1174 and 1175 he made treaties with Genoa and Venice and his marriage in February 1177 with J
2 CONC oan, daughter of Henry II of England and Eleanor of Aquitaine, marks his high position in European politics.
