1 NOTE Peter I (Portuguese: Pedro, pron. IPA: ['ped?u]) was the second son of King Sancho I of Portugal and his wife Dulce Berenguer, infanta of Aragon. He was Count of Urgell by marriage to Countess Aurembiaix of Urgell, and after her d
2 CONC eath occupied the same position in a titular capacity. He was also Lord of the Balearic Islands. He was born in Coimbra on February 23, 1187. Pedro also lived in León. He died on June 2, 1258
