0 @N6000000002188376628@ NOTE Infanta Beatriz, Countess of Alburquerque
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Infanta Beatriz of Portugal (pron. IPA: [bi?'t?i?]; English: Beatrice or Beatrix) was the daughter of Portuguese King Peter I and a Castilian noblewoman called Inês de Castro that had arrived in Portugal as a maid of Constance of 
1 CONC Penafiel, recently married to Pedro I (Heir Prince at the time).
1 CONT
1 CONT Beatrice was born in Coimbra around the period of 1347-1351 and she became Countess of Alburquerque when she married Sancho, Count of Alburquerque. She died in 1381.
1 CONT
1 CONT Beatrice's entitlement to be considered an Infanta of Portugal is debatable. Some historians consider her a natural daughter of Peter I, so the title Infanta of Portugal could never be attributed to her. Other opinions refer that 
1 CONC after the death of Inês de Castro, ordered by Pedro's father King Afonso IV of Portugal, the Prince after inheriting the throne admitted that he had married Inês secretly, and because of that she was a lawful Queen of Portugal.
1 CONT
1 CONT Of Inês de Castro, Peter I had two sons and a daughter:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * (Infanta) Beatrice of Portugal (1347/1351-1381)
1 CONT     * (Infante) John of Portugal (1349-1387)
1 CONT     * (Infante) Denis of Portugal (1354-1397)
0 @N6000000002322303437@ NOTE This marriage also caused unrest because there were no male heirs to the
1 CONT throne of Portugal, only Beatriz. This would be the end of this dynasty, and
1 CONT the house of Avis would take over from this time in history.
0 @N6000000002322303426@ NOTE This lady of somewhat doubtful morals, provoked discontent amongst the royal
1 CONT subjects and the nobility.
0 @N6000000002176654650@ NOTE This marriage also caused unrest because there were no male heirs to the
1 CONT throne of Portugal, only Beatriz. This would be the end of this dynasty, and
1 CONT the house of Avis would take over from this time in history.
0 @N6000000002176654640@ NOTE This lady of somewhat doubtful morals, provoked discontent amongst the royal
1 CONT subjects and the nobility.
0 @N6000000002188376733@ NOTE Leonor Telles de Menezes
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Dona Leonor (Elionor) Telles (Teles) de Menezes (Meneses) (1350 - April 27, 1386), called by the people at her time a Aleivosa ("The Treacherous"), was queen consort of Portugal during the 14th century. Born in Trás-os-Montes e Al
1 CONC to Douro, she served as queen consort from 1372 to 1383 and as regent from 1383 to 1384.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married at a young age to a courtier named Dom João Lourenço da Cunha, 3rd Senhor de Pombeiro, with whom she had a son, Dom Álvaro da Cunha, she would be seduced by Ferdinand I of Portugal when he was a prince. This would occur wh
1 CONC ile Leonor was visiting her sister Maria Telles, lady-in-waiting to Ferdinand's half-sister Infanta Beatrice of Portugal.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ferdinand managed to annul her first marriage to João Lourenço da Cunha on grounds of consanguinity and on May 5, 1372 secretly married Leonor Telles de Menezes.
1 CONT
1 CONT Upon the death of Ferdinand (1383), Leonor was nominated regent in the name of her daughter Beatrice (Beatriz). From 1383 onwards, Leonor ruled with her lover, João Fernandes Andeiro, 2nd Conde de Ourém, called Conde Andeiro, whic
1 CONC h angered the nobility and the lower classes. Beatrice's marriage to the Castilian king John I led to the expulsion of both mother and daughter.
1 CONT
1 CONT The loss of independence had been unthinkable for the majority of Portuguese nobles. A rebellion led by the Master of the Order of Aviz, future João I of Portugal, started in that year, leading to the 1383-1385 Crisis.
1 CONT
1 CONT She died in exile at a monastery at Tordesillas.
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Beatrice of Castile Queen Consort of Portugal
1 CONT 5 May 1372 - 22 October 1383 Succeeded by
1 CONT John I of Castile
0 @N6000000002240794437@ NOTE This marriage also caused unrest because there were no male heirs to the
1 CONT throne of Portugal, only Beatriz. This would be the end of this dynasty, and
1 CONT the house of Avis would take over from this time in history.
