0 @N6000000002322298254@ NOTE An illegitimate son of Duke Roger of Apulia and grandson of Roger II, his
1 CONT brief reign marked the end of the Norman rule in Sicily. Tancred joined an
1 CONT insurrection against his uncle William I of Sicily in 1155 and was imprisoned
1 CONT for five years. Released, he participated in another abortive coup in 1161
1 CONT and went into exile. 13 years later he was forgiven by William II and found
1 CONT himself heir upon the death of William II. Opposed by the barons but backed
1 CONT by the people and papacy, he was crowned king in 1190. See William III.
